IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
-- EVERY-EACH-QUANTIFIER-SPEC §5.1.1 (R-Q7A/B/C, RULED 2026-09-07, BUILT
-- 2026-09-15): the ANCHORED deadline, `WITHIN d OF anchor`.
--
-- Unanchored, a WITHIN counts from where the language puts it: under HENCE,
-- the join's firing (§5.1); under LEST, today, the event that revealed the
-- miss (§5.2 owes the missed deadline). Anchored, it is ABSOLUTE — the
-- anchor's instant plus d — and the anchor is one of
--
--   OF THE JOIN        the instant the ENCLOSING obligation's join fired
--   OF THE DEADLINE    the enclosing obligation's deadline
--   OF THE ARMING      the instant the enclosing obligation was entered
--   OF e               an instant: a NUMBER on the trace's clock, or a DATE
--
-- where "enclosing" means the obligation whose HENCE or LEST this one is the
-- continuation of — the one it is ATTACHED to when it runs (the section "A
-- continuation that arrives as a value" pins that). Every trace below pins
-- one anchor to a number, and the number the breach reports is the deadline
-- the anchor produced.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Landlord HAS name IS A STRING
    Tenant   HAS name IS A STRING

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Sign    HAS signer IS AN Actor
    Deliver HAS who    IS AN Actor
    Refund  HAS who    IS AN Actor
    Smoke   HAS who    IS AN Actor

theLandlord MEANS Landlord OF "Ms Ng"
alice       MEANS Tenant OF "Alice"
bob         MEANS Tenant OF "Bob"
tenants     MEANS LIST alice, bob


§ `OF THE JOIN is the HENCE default, said out loud`

-- The landlord's five days run from Alice's signature — exactly as they would
-- with no anchor at all (run-barrier.l4 pins the unanchored form to the same
-- arithmetic). A delivery at day 13 is timely; the breach at 14 reports the
-- deadline 8 + 5 = 13.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`of the join` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 30
    HENCE (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 5 OF THE JOIN)
    LEST  BREACH

#TRACE `of the join` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 8
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 13

#TRACE `of the join` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 8
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 14


§ `OF THE DEADLINE under HENCE: the cure period runs from when performance fell due`

-- Alice signs early, at day 8, but the landlord's five days count from day
-- 30, when her signature fell due — not from day 8. Delivery at 35 is timely;
-- the breach at 36 reports 30 + 5 = 35.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`of the deadline` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 30
    HENCE (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 5 OF THE DEADLINE)
    LEST  BREACH

#TRACE `of the deadline` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 8
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 35

#TRACE `of the deadline` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 8
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 36


§ `OF THE DEADLINE under LEST: the cure period runs from the missed deadline`

-- Alice misses day 10. The miss is revealed by her late signature at day 14,
-- and today's UNANCHORED rule would start her cure period there (§5.2 records
-- that as the change still owed). Anchored, the cure period runs from the
-- deadline she missed: 10 + 5 = 15, whatever day the miss came to light. Her
-- signature at 14 is re-offered to the LEST and discharges it; a signature at
-- 16 does not, and the breach reports 15.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`cure from the deadline` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 10
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  (PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 5 OF THE DEADLINE)

#TRACE `cure from the deadline` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 14

#TRACE `cure from the deadline` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 16


§ `OF THE ARMING: within so many days of the agreement, two levels down`

-- Three obligations in a chain. The landlord delivers (armed at 0); then Bob
-- signs (armed at the delivery); then Alice signs WITHIN 40 OF THE ARMING.
-- THE ARMING is the arming of the ENCLOSING obligation — Bob's, which was
-- entered when the landlord delivered, at day 5 — so Alice's deadline is
-- 5 + 40 = 45, not 20 + 40 = 60 (her own arming) and not 0 + 40 (the
-- outermost rule's). The nearest enclosing obligation is the one an anchor
-- names.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`of the arming` MEANS
    PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 10
    HENCE (PARTY bob MUST Sign (EXACTLY bob) WITHIN 30
           HENCE (PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 40 OF THE ARMING))
    LEST  BREACH

#TRACE `of the arming` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 5
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 20
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 45

#TRACE `of the arming` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 5
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 20
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 46

-- At the top level there is no enclosing obligation, and THE ARMING is the
-- obligation's own arming: the default, allowed and pointless. Armed at 3,
-- due 3 + 7 = 10.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`own arming` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 7 OF THE ARMING

#TRACE `own arming` AT 3 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 11


§ `OF an instant: a NUMBER on the trace's clock, or a DATE`

closingDate MEANS 20

-- A NUMBER is an instant on the trace's own scale, whatever the obligation's
-- clock read when it was entered: armed at 3, due 20 + 5 = 25.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`of a number` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 5 OF closingDate

#TRACE `of a number` AT 3 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 26

-- A DATE is lowered to its serial (DATE_SERIAL), so on a trace whose clock is
-- date serials it means the calendar date: WITHIN 0 OF 30 June 2026 is
-- "by 30 June". A signature on 1 July reports the deadline as the serial of
-- 30 June 2026.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`by thirty june` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 0 OF (YMD 2026 6 30)

#TRACE `by thirty june` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 6 1)) WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 6 30))

#TRACE `by thirty june` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 6 1)) WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 7 1))

-- Already expired at arming: the contract begins on 1 July and the deadline
-- was five days after 20 June. That is not an error; the first event reveals
-- the expiry, and the breach reports the deadline that had already passed.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`already expired` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 5 OF (YMD 2026 6 20)

#TRACE `already expired` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 7 1)) WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 7 2))

-- The duration is any NUMBER expression; in the WITHIN slot OF is the anchor,
-- so an applied duration is bracketed (or written with juxtaposed arguments,
-- `twice 3`). Due 0 + 6 = 6.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER GIVETH A NUMBER DECIDE twice n IS n TIMES 2

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`applied duration` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN (twice OF 3) OF THE ARMING

#TRACE `applied duration` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 7


§ `Under a barrier`

-- THE DEADLINE in a barrier's HENCE is the ONCE line's WITHIN when one is
-- written — the deadline on the whole (R-T2) — and otherwise the latest of
-- the members' act deadlines, the instant by which all performance fell
-- due. Here there is no ONCE-line WITHIN: every member was due at 14, so
-- the landlord's five days run from 14, not from Bob's signature at 9.
-- Delivery at 19 is timely; at 20 the breach reports 14 + 5 = 19.
--
-- Under the barrier's LEST, THE DEADLINE is the deadline that was actually
-- missed — here the failing member's: Bob's, at 14. The refund is due
-- 14 + 5 = 19 whether the miss came to light at day 15 or day 20.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`the tenancy` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN tenants
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
        WITHIN 14
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 5 OF THE DEADLINE)
        LEST   (PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund  (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 5 OF THE DEADLINE)

#TRACE `the tenancy` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 9
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 19

#TRACE `the tenancy` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 9
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 20

#TRACE `the tenancy` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 20

-- With a WITHIN on the ONCE line, THE DEADLINE in the HENCE is that one:
-- the group's deadline, 30, so delivery is due 30 + 5 = 35.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`the tenancy, bounded as a whole` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN tenants
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
        WITHIN 14
        ONCE   ALL HAVE WITHIN 30
        HENCE  (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 5 OF THE DEADLINE)
        LEST   BREACH

#TRACE `the tenancy, bounded as a whole` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 9
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 36

-- With BOTH layers written, THE DEADLINE under the LEST is whichever was
-- actually missed. Bob misses his act deadline, 14, and his late signature
-- at 15 reveals it: the refund runs from 14, not from the group's 30 — due
-- 14 + 5 = 19, so a refund at 20 breaches reporting 19.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`the tenancy, a member late` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN tenants
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
        WITHIN 14
        ONCE   ALL HAVE WITHIN 30
        HENCE  FULFILLED
        LEST   (PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 5 OF THE DEADLINE)

#TRACE `the tenancy, a member late` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 15
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 20

-- And the other layer: every member signs within the act's 40, but the last
-- signature, at 31, lands after the ONCE line's 30. That is the deadline
-- the LEST counts from: 30 + 5 = 35, so a refund at 36 breaches reporting 35.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`the tenancy, the group late` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN tenants
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
        WITHIN 40
        ONCE   ALL HAVE WITHIN 30
        HENCE  FULFILLED
        LEST   (PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 5 OF THE DEADLINE)

#TRACE `the tenancy, the group late` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 31
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 36

-- Members may be due at different times. THE DEADLINE in the HENCE is then
-- the LATEST of their deadlines — when all performance had fallen due —
-- and not the deadline of whoever happened to complete last, so the order
-- the roll names them in cannot move it. Alice is due at 20, Bob at 10;
-- both have signed by day 9, so the landlord's five days run from 20:
-- delivery at 25 is timely, and at 26 the breach reports 25 — from either
-- roll, and whether or not the two signatures share a stamp.
GIVEN t IS AN Actor GIVETH A NUMBER
grace t MEANS
    CONSIDER t
    WHEN Tenant n   THEN (IF n EQUALS "Alice" THEN 20 ELSE 10)
    WHEN Landlord n THEN 0

GIVEN roll IS A LIST OF Actor
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`per member` roll MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN roll
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
        WITHIN grace t
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 5 OF THE DEADLINE)
        LEST   BREACH

#TRACE `per member` (LIST alice, bob) AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 5
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 9
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 25

#TRACE `per member` (LIST alice, bob) AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 9
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 9
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 26

#TRACE `per member` (LIST bob, alice) AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 9
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 9
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 26

-- A barrier over NOBODY is joined at its arming — "all zero of them have
-- acted" is true at once — and its HENCE fires there. THE DEADLINE in that
-- HENCE is the ONCE line's WITHIN when written: 0 + 30, so delivery is due
-- 35 and the breach at 36 reports 35.
nobody MEANS LIST

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`nobody, bounded as a whole` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN nobody
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
        ONCE   ALL HAVE WITHIN 30
        HENCE  (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 5 OF THE DEADLINE)
        LEST   BREACH

#TRACE `nobody, bounded as a whole` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 36

-- With only an act WITHIN, nobody had a deadline to meet, so there is none
-- for THE DEADLINE to name: the run refuses and says so — also when the
-- EVERY sits under an obligation that has a deadline of its own, which is
-- NOT borrowed (the landlord's 10 here plays no part).
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`nobody, act deadline only` MEANS
    PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 10
    HENCE (EVERY Tenant t IN nobody
              MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
              WITHIN 3
              ONCE   ALL HAVE
              HENCE  (PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 5 OF THE DEADLINE)
              LEST   BREACH)
    LEST  BREACH

#TRACE `nobody, act deadline only` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 2
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 16

-- A join line's own WITHIN may be anchored too — to THE ARMING (the EVERY's
-- own arming, which is also what it counts from unanchored) or to an
-- instant; not to THE JOIN or THE DEADLINE, which it is what defines. Here
-- the EVERY is nested under the landlord's delivery, so it is armed at day 5,
-- and its members are due 5 + 14 = 19: Bob's signature at 20 breaches.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`after delivery` MEANS
    PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 10
    HENCE (EVERY Tenant t IN tenants
              MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
              ONCE   ALL HAVE WITHIN 14 OF THE ARMING
              HENCE  FULFILLED
              LEST   BREACH)
    LEST  BREACH

#TRACE `after delivery` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 5
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 6
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 19

#TRACE `after delivery` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 5
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 6
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 20

-- The whole group must have signed by instant 105 (100 + 5), whatever day
-- the EVERY was armed. That is the state deadline, and — as a join-line
-- WITHIN written alone always does (R-T2) — it also bounds each act, so it
-- is what the LEST's THE DEADLINE names: the refund is due 105 + 1 = 106.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`by instant 105` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN tenants
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
        ONCE   ALL HAVE WITHIN 5 OF 100
        HENCE  FULFILLED
        LEST   (PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 1 OF THE DEADLINE)

#TRACE `by instant 105` AT 3 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 4
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 105

#TRACE `by instant 105` AT 3 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 4
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 106
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 107


§ `Under a fork`

-- Each member's HENCE is its own continuation, and THE DEADLINE in it is
-- that member's deadline. Both tenants were due at 14, so both deliveries
-- are due 14 + 2 = 16 — the one Alice's signature at 1 spawned no earlier
-- than the one Bob's at 9 did. A delivery at 17 breaches both; the compound
-- is anchored at the first and names both (R-T3), each with its 16.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`receipts` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN tenants
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
        WITHIN 14
        UPON   EACH
        HENCE  (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 2 OF THE DEADLINE)
        LEST   BREACH BY t

#TRACE `receipts` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 9
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 17


§ `A continuation that arrives as a value`

-- The anchors name the obligation a continuation is ATTACHED to when it
-- runs, not the one it happens to be written under. `after k` is Bob's
-- obligation with k as its HENCE; the landlord's obligation is written
-- under Alice's HENCE and handed to `after`, so when it runs it is Bob's
-- continuation. OF THE JOIN is Bob's signature at 50 — the same instant an
-- unanchored WITHIN 5 in that place counts from — so delivery at 55 is
-- timely and at 56 the breach reports 55; OF THE DEADLINE is Bob's
-- deadline, 3 + 100 = 103, so delivery at 108 is timely and at 109 the
-- breach reports 108. (The checker sees only where an anchor is WRITTEN,
-- so it refuses THE JOIN and THE DEADLINE at the top level and in a WHERE;
-- a value carrying THE JOIN that is later attached under a LEST is refused
-- when it runs, not before.)
GIVEN k IS A DEONTIC Actor Action
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
after k MEANS
    PARTY bob MUST Sign (EXACTLY bob) WITHIN 100
    HENCE k
    LEST  BREACH

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`handed on, the join` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 10
    HENCE (after (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 5 OF THE JOIN))
    LEST  BREACH

#TRACE `handed on, the join` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 3
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 50
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 55

#TRACE `handed on, the join` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 3
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 50
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 56

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`handed on, the deadline` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 10
    HENCE (after (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 5 OF THE DEADLINE))
    LEST  BREACH

#TRACE `handed on, the deadline` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 3
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 50
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 108

#TRACE `handed on, the deadline` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 3
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 50
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 109

-- Inside a compound the rule is the same. `afterBoth k` attaches k as ONE
-- operand of the `RAND` in its HENCE, and k is still Bob's continuation:
-- OF THE JOIN is Bob's signature at 50 and OF THE DEADLINE is 103, exactly
-- as under `after` — delivery at 55 / 108 is timely, and at 56 / 109 the
-- breach reports 55 / 108. An operand is handed off when the compound is
-- applied, one operand at a time, so a value inside a compound anchors to
-- the obligation the compound is attached to (spec §5.1.1.1, "Threading").
GIVEN k IS A DEONTIC Actor Action
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
afterBoth k MEANS
    PARTY bob MUST Sign (EXACTLY bob) WITHIN 100
    HENCE (k RAND (PARTY bob MUST Refund (EXACTLY bob) WITHIN 100))
    LEST  BREACH

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`handed on, in a compound, the join` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 10
    HENCE (afterBoth (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 5 OF THE JOIN))
    LEST  BREACH

#TRACE `handed on, in a compound, the join` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 3
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 50
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 55
  PARTY bob   DOES Refund bob AT 60

#TRACE `handed on, in a compound, the join` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 3
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 50
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 56
  PARTY bob   DOES Refund bob AT 60

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`handed on, in a compound, the deadline` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 10
    HENCE (afterBoth (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 5 OF THE DEADLINE))
    LEST  BREACH

#TRACE `handed on, in a compound, the deadline` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 3
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 50
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 108
  PARTY bob   DOES Refund bob AT 110

#TRACE `handed on, in a compound, the deadline` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 3
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 50
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 109
  PARTY bob   DOES Refund bob AT 110

-- `ROR` the same: delivery at 55 is timely, and one alternative met is enough.
GIVEN k IS A DEONTIC Actor Action
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
afterEither k MEANS
    PARTY bob MUST Sign (EXACTLY bob) WITHIN 100
    HENCE (k ROR (PARTY bob MUST Refund (EXACTLY bob) WITHIN 100))
    LEST  BREACH

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`handed on, either way` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 10
    HENCE (afterEither (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 5 OF THE JOIN))
    LEST  BREACH

#TRACE `handed on, either way` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 3
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 50
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 55

-- A WHERE local is the same case. `cure` is defined outside the HENCE and
-- attached to Alice's obligation when her HENCE fires, so OF THE ARMING is
-- Alice's arming, 0, exactly as if `cure` had been written inline: the
-- deadline is 5, and delivery at 6 breaches reporting 5. Factoring an
-- inline continuation out into a WHERE does not move its deadline — nor
-- does putting the local inside a compound.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`factored out` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 10
    HENCE cure
    LEST  BREACH
    WHERE
      cure MEANS PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 5 OF THE ARMING

#TRACE `factored out` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 3
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 6

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`factored out, in a compound` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 10
    HENCE (cure RAND (PARTY bob MUST Sign (EXACTLY bob) WITHIN 100))
    LEST  BREACH
    WHERE
      cure MEANS PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 5 OF THE ARMING

#TRACE `factored out, in a compound` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 3
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 6
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 7

-- What a value may NOT be attached to. The checker sees only where an
-- anchor is written, so it lets THE JOIN and THE DEADLINE through here:
-- both are written under Alice's HENCE, which has a WITHIN. The run refuses
-- them where they are attached — THE JOIN under a LEST, whose join never
-- fired, and THE DEADLINE under an obligation that has no WITHIN — and a
-- compound does not hide the attachment.
GIVEN k IS A DEONTIC Actor Action
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
unless k MEANS
    PARTY bob MUST Sign (EXACTLY bob) WITHIN 10
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  k

GIVEN k IS A DEONTIC Actor Action
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
unlessBoth k MEANS
    PARTY bob MUST Sign (EXACTLY bob) WITHIN 10
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  (k RAND (PARTY bob MUST Refund (EXACTLY bob) WITHIN 100))

GIVEN k IS A DEONTIC Actor Action
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`after, open-ended` k MEANS
    PARTY bob MUST Sign (EXACTLY bob)
    HENCE k

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`handed under a LEST` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 10
    HENCE (unless (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 5 OF THE JOIN))
    LEST  BREACH

#TRACE `handed under a LEST` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 3
  PARTY bob   DOES Smoke bob   AT 14
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 18

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`handed under a LEST, in a compound` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 10
    HENCE (unlessBoth (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 5 OF THE JOIN))
    LEST  BREACH

#TRACE `handed under a LEST, in a compound` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 3
  PARTY bob   DOES Smoke bob   AT 14
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 18
  PARTY bob   DOES Refund bob AT 20

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`handed to no WITHIN` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 10
    HENCE (`after, open-ended` (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 5 OF THE DEADLINE))
    LEST  BREACH

#TRACE `handed to no WITHIN` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 3
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 50
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 60


§ `A prohibition kept: the join is the event that revealed it`

-- Alice must not smoke for ten days. Nothing happens on day 10 itself; the
-- machine learns the prohibition was kept when the next event arrives, and
-- that revealing event is where the HENCE's clock starts when the WITHIN is
-- unanchored or anchored OF THE JOIN: below, Bob's signature at 30 reveals
-- it, so delivery is due 33 and at 34 the breach reports 33. To count from
-- the day the prohibition was discharged instead, anchor to THE DEADLINE:
-- 10 + 3 = 13, whatever event reveals the kept prohibition — in the second
-- trace the landlord's own delivery at 14 is that event, and it is already
-- late, reporting 13.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`kept, the join` MEANS
    PARTY alice SHANT Smoke (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 10
    HENCE (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 3 OF THE JOIN)
    LEST  BREACH

#TRACE `kept, the join` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY bob DOES Sign bob AT 30
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 34

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`kept, the deadline` MEANS
    PARTY alice SHANT Smoke (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 10
    HENCE (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 3 OF THE DEADLINE)
    LEST  BREACH

#TRACE `kept, the deadline` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 14


§ `What a residual prints`

-- An obligation that has not met an event prints its deadline as written,
-- anchor and all. One that has prints the days remaining: the landlord's
-- deadline was fixed at 30 + 5 = 35 when Bob's (irrelevant) signature at day
-- 20 was scrutinised, and 15 days remain. The anchor was resolved once, at
-- that first event, and is spent.
#EVAL `of the join`

#TRACE `of the deadline` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 8

#TRACE `of the deadline` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 8
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 20

-- An inline rule, so the natural-language linearisation of an anchor
-- ("within 7 of the arming") is in this file's .nlg golden too.
#EVAL PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 7 OF THE ARMING
